{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "slug": "excel-averageif-122",
  "trackId": "excel",
  "code": "EX-122",
  "title": "Average per store with AVERAGEIF",
  "summary": "Find the average sales per store for one region with AVERAGEIF and compare it with the company average.",
  "estimatedMinutes": 15,
  "level": "intermediate",
  "passMark": 0.75,
  "exerciseId": "averageif-region-average",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "briefing",
      "title": "Briefing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A regional total can mislead. Nairobi may sell more than Kisumu simply because it has more stores. To compare fairly you need the average sales per store in each region."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "AVERAGEIF works like SUMIF, but it returns the average of the matching rows instead of the total."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Objective: calculate the average of one group with AVERAGEIF.",
            "Time: about 15 minutes.",
            "You pass the mission at 75% or more in the Assessment."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "training",
      "title": "Training",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "formula": "=AVERAGEIF(range, criteria, [average_range])",
          "text": "Look down range for cells that match criteria, then average the numbers on the same rows of average_range. The two ranges must be the same size."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "Sales list in A1:C7 (sales in K)",
          "columns": [
            "Row",
            "A: Store",
            "B: Region",
            "C: Sales (K)"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "2",
              "Westlands",
              "Nairobi",
              "120"
            ],
            [
              "3",
              "Nyali",
              "Mombasa",
              "85"
            ],
            [
              "4",
              "Karen",
              "Nairobi",
              "150"
            ],
            [
              "5",
              "Bamburi",
              "Mombasa",
              "92"
            ],
            [
              "6",
              "Kondele",
              "Kisumu",
              "64"
            ],
            [
              "7",
              "Kilimani",
              "Nairobi",
              "90"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "formula": "=AVERAGEIF(B2:B7,\"Kisumu\",C2:C7)",
          "text": "Only one Kisumu store matches (Kondele, 64), so the average is 64K. An average of one number is that number."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "AVERAGEIF is the matching total divided by the matching count: the same as SUMIF divided by COUNTIF.",
            "If no row matches, there is nothing to average and Excel shows #DIV/0!.",
            "Compare with AVERAGE(C2:C7), which averages every row whatever the region.",
            "Use $ signs on the ranges and a cell for the criteria so the formula can be copied down."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "simulation",
      "title": "Simulation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "excel-grid"
        },
        {
          "type": "exercise-hints"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "assessment",
      "title": "Assessment",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Use the sales list from Training (A1:C7). Round answers to 1 decimal place, for example 12.3."
        },
        {
          "type": "assessment-items",
          "itemIds": [
            "l1-nairobi-average",
            "l2-mombasa-average",
            "l3-no-match",
            "l4-same-as"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "debrief",
      "title": "Debrief",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "AVERAGEIF(range, criteria, average_range) averages only the matching rows.",
            "It equals the matching total divided by the matching count.",
            "No matching row gives #DIV/0!.",
            "Compare a region average with the all-store average to see who is above or below."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Averages per store let you compare regions of different sizes fairly."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "assessment": {
    "items": [
      {
        "id": "l1-nairobi-average",
        "type": "numeric",
        "prompt": "What does =AVERAGEIF(B2:B7,\"Nairobi\",C2:C7) return, in K?",
        "answerHint": "To 1 decimal place, in K"
      },
      {
        "id": "l2-mombasa-average",
        "type": "numeric",
        "prompt": "What does =AVERAGEIF(B2:B7,\"Mombasa\",C2:C7) return, in K?",
        "answerHint": "To 1 decimal place, in K"
      },
      {
        "id": "l3-no-match",
        "type": "single-choice",
        "prompt": "What does =AVERAGEIF(B2:B7,\"Eldoret\",C2:C7) show when there is no Eldoret store in the list?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "zero",
            "label": "0"
          },
          {
            "id": "div0",
            "label": "#DIV/0!"
          },
          {
            "id": "na",
            "label": "#N/A"
          },
          {
            "id": "all",
            "label": "The average of all stores"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "l4-same-as",
        "type": "single-choice",
        "prompt": "Which formula gives the same answer as =AVERAGEIF(B2:B7,\"Nairobi\",C2:C7)?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "sumif-countif",
            "label": "SUMIF(B2:B7,\"Nairobi\",C2:C7)/COUNTIF(B2:B7,\"Nairobi\")"
          },
          {
            "id": "sumif-count",
            "label": "SUMIF(B2:B7,\"Nairobi\",C2:C7)/COUNT(C2:C7)"
          },
          {
            "id": "average-all",
            "label": "AVERAGE(C2:C7)"
          },
          {
            "id": "countif-sales",
            "label": "SUMIF(B2:B7,\"Nairobi\",C2:C7)/COUNTIF(C2:C7,\"Nairobi\")"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
